From: vi_asr team
Subject: [PATCH] feat(encoder): add non-reentrant activation checkpointing and lazy model import

1. Enable torch.utils.checkpoint.checkpoint with use_reentrant=False in
   ChunkFormerEncoder.forward_layers to reduce activation memory on dual T4.
2. Bind layer per-iteration via closure helper make_custom_forward.
3. Lazy-load ChunkFormerModel in chunkformer/__init__.py to prevent eager top-level dependency errors.
---
 chunkformer/__init__.py        |  7 +++++-
 chunkformer/modules/encoder.py | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chunkformer/__init__.py b/chunkformer/__init__.py
index 9fda618..55f4ebc 100644
--- a/chunkformer/__init__.py
+++ b/chunkformer/__init__.py
@@ -9,6 +9,11 @@ __version__ = "1.2.2"
 __author__ = "khanld"
 __email__ = "khanhld218@gmail.com"
 
-from chunkformer.chunkformer_model import ChunkFormerModel
+def __getattr__(name: str):
+    if name == "ChunkFormerModel":
+        from chunkformer.chunkformer_model import ChunkFormerModel
+        return ChunkFormerModel
+    raise AttributeError(f"module {__name__!r} has no attribute {name!r}")
+
 
 __all__ = ["ChunkFormerModel", "__version__"]
diff --git a/chunkformer/modules/encoder.py b/chunkformer/modules/encoder.py
